### discuss-feature

Before beginning, ask the developer to consider committing any prior changes to the project to source control before continuing.

Follow these steps:

1. Read the project spec index at `{{ $baseDir }}/{{ $specFolder }}/{{ $specIndexName }}` and skim any domain specs relevant to the developer's request. Also briefly explore the codebase to understand what already exists (entry points, directory structure, key modules).
2. Ask the developer clarifying questions about their request. Focus on:
   - What problem this feature solves and who it's for
   - Expected behavior and edge cases
   - How it interacts with existing functionality
   - Any constraints (performance, compatibility, dependencies)

   After each response, state your confidence level (0-100%) in understanding what the developer wants to build. Continue asking questions until you reach at least 85% confidence.
3. After reaching >85% confidence, present a brief summary of your understanding — including any gaps you filled with assumptions. Ask the developer to confirm, correct, or continue refining.
4. After confirmation, write the agreed requirements to `{{ $baseDir }}/{{ $planFileName }}` using this structure:

```markdown
## Feature: <name>

### Problem
What problem this solves and why it matters.

### Requirements
- Requirement 1
- Requirement 2

### Assumptions
- Any gaps filled with sensible defaults (noted so spec-plan can verify).

### Affected Areas
Which parts of the codebase this feature touches (modules, packages, layers).
```

{{ if .IsMultiProject -}}
#### Multi-Project Context

This is a multi-project workspace. When exploring the codebase:

1. Read child project specs (listed in the Multi-Project Context section above) for cross-service context.
2. Consider how the feature may span multiple services and note cross-service dependencies in the Affected Areas section.
{{ end -}}

#### Criteria

- [ ] Requirements written to {{ $baseDir }}/{{ $planFileName }} using the structure above
- [ ] Assumptions are explicitly called out
- [ ] Developer confirms the plan
